          "title": "Belle Flux et Trente et Un",
          "subtitle": "Vying",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Belle, Flux et Trente-et-Un is a historical French-German gambling game combining three scoring contests: belle, flux, and thirty-one."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A seventeenth and eighteenth century gambling game related to Brag, Poch, and early poker ancestry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2-8 players use the table arrangement described for Belle Flux et Trente et Un."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "French-suited pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "French-suited pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal hands for the three contests, then resolve the best belle, flush, and thirty-one claims against the stakes."
            }
